# Finding the Longest Unique Substring

To solve this problem, I'll write a method that finds the longest substring with no repeating characters. Let's approach this step by step:

```java
public static String longestUniqueSubstring(String s) {
    // Handle edge cases
    if (s == null || s.isEmpty()) {
        return "";
    }

    String longestSoFar = "";

    // Check all possible substrings
    for (int startIndex = 0; startIndex < s.length(); startIndex++) {
        // For each starting position, try to find the longest unique substring
        StringBuilder currentSubstring = new StringBuilder();
        boolean[] charUsed = new boolean[128]; // Assuming ASCII characters

        for (int endIndex = startIndex; endIndex < s.length(); endIndex++) {
            char currentChar = s.charAt(endIndex);

            // If character is already used, we've found a repeat
            if (charUsed[currentChar]) {
                break;
            }

            // Add character to current substring and mark it as used
            currentSubstring.append(currentChar);
            charUsed[currentChar] = true;

            // Update longest if current is longer
            if (currentSubstring.length() > longestSoFar.length()) {
                longestSoFar = currentSubstring.toString();
            }
        }
    }

    return longestSoFar;
}
```

